  "target_module": "amphora-molecule-property",
  "theory": "Lorentz-Lorenz (1880): (n^2-1)/(n^2+2) = R_LL*rho/M, with R_LL an ADDITIVE sum of Eisenlohr/Vogel atomic+bond refractions (Van Krevelen Properties of Polymers ch.10). n_pred = sqrt((1+2f)/(1-f)), f=R_LL*rho/M. R_LL constants are pure literature values (NOT fitted to this set) -> non-circular. Refractive index drives coating hiding-power/opacity via pigment-vs-binder RI contrast, gloss, and refractometric incoming QC; R_LL is also the electronic-polarization term of Clausius-Mossotti (n^2 ~ high-frequency permittivity), linking RI to film barrier physics.",
